WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.880
- All right, here we go,
this is the Rubin Report.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.616
I'm still Dave Rubin and I have a feeling

00:00:08.616 --> 00:00:11.420
that YouTube may not be
thrilled with this episode,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.000
so even more reason to
subscribe and click that bell

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.740
so that you actually get
notified when the clips come out.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.810
And joining me today is the
VP of the Trump Organization

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.290
and the author of the new book, Triggered.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.590
Donald Trump, Jr., welcome
to The Rubin Report.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:27.030
- Good to be with you, buddy.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:28.160
- All right, here we go, man.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.000
I'm 50-50 on whether this
stream is going to be up

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.020
by the time I finish this
very sentence right now.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:33.853
What do you think?

00:00:33.853 --> 00:00:34.686
- It's sort of a win either way, right?

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:36.461
If they censor you we can blow it up

00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:39.020
and make it go everywhere
then other people will watch.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.890
But it's a shame that we even have to have

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.010
that conversation.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:43.870
- It's sort of ridiculous,
we're gonna get to that.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.970
And that actually has a lot to
do with what you write about

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.930
in the book here, about
all the tech censorship

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:48.763
and all that stuff.

00:00:48.763 --> 00:00:50.540
But before we do any of that,

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:51.950
I don't know if you
remember but a couple days

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:54.330
you were on The View,
that View program on ABC.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.360
- I don't remember that.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.510
No one's mentioned that to me since.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:57.460
- Do you remember that?

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.660
So there were so many things that happened

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.620
in that interview that I was like holy cow

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.220
this is everything that
I talk about all at once.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.300
So let's just try to hit a
couple things in a row here.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.367
First off, the way the
interview started where Whoopi,

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.660
who I used to really like Whoopi.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.450
I think she used to be a decent liberal

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.610
and now she kind of gone off
the progressive deep end.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.030
She couldn't even say
your name in the intro.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.060
She literally refused to say your name.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.010
What does that feel like when you sit down

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.560
and you know you're in enemy territory?

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.970
And then the way they treat you

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.480
before anything has happened?

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.349
- Well listen, it obviously
shows just how disingenuous

00:01:31.349 --> 00:01:32.747
the whole thing is first
and foremost, right?

00:01:32.747 --> 00:01:35.973
I mean they invite you on
to talk about your book.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.020
Did you hear a question?

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.244
I did three segments.

00:01:40.244 --> 00:01:43.420
I'm not a baby, like I
get I'm gonna get hit.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:46.230
I get that in that case there's not even

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:51.027
a conservative on my
side, given the history.

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:53.300
- Meghan's there, but she's not really.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.835
- Abby Huntsman's sort of, what are you?

00:01:54.835 --> 00:01:57.220
There's not a lot of personality there

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:58.053
for that kind of stuff.

00:01:58.053 --> 00:02:01.600
So I get it, I get that I'm
going into the lion's den.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.720
But come on, they're gonna
lecture me about civility?

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.840
But you have me on for
a pretense, the book.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:12.200
You don't ask me a single
question about the book

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.944
and you refuse to even
mention my last name?

00:02:14.944 --> 00:02:17.785
This is going wrong real
fast, but that's okay.

00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:20.940
- So she basically said
the son of the President.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.390
Then she kind of choked out DJT.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.370
- Don, Jr., I think or
Donald, Junior, she said.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.719
But she never said Trump.

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:30.330
I'm like it's okay, I guess people know.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.340
But what's the pur--, what does it serve?

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.118
- Yeah, but it does set a certain tone

00:02:34.118 --> 00:02:35.500
that's been consistent.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:36.983
I mean Rand Paul was on
there a couple weeks ago

00:02:36.983 --> 00:02:39.000
and the way that they were treating him.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.540
But then a few things happened in a row

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:42.500
that I thought were pretty interesting.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.610
So you started getting
hit and you apparently

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:46.690
had done a little research,

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.170
'cause you turned the question
around and said to Joy,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.560
you know Joy, you've been in Blackface.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.520
And now Joy has been in Blackface,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.300
she has admitted it on The View.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.870
She immediately says she hasn't.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.470
Whoopi then said, well I'm a Black woman

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:00.689
and I know what Blackface is.

00:03:00.689 --> 00:03:03.910
- And Whoopi, and you
supported Roman Polanski,

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:05.257
a child rapist.

00:03:05.257 --> 00:03:07.933
- It's not rape rape,
that's what she said.

00:03:07.933 --> 00:03:09.350
- You know, yeah you're right.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.460
Sodomy of a 13, 14-year
old girl under Quaaludes,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.780
you're right that's not rape, Whoopi.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.080
If that's not rape I don't know what is.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.720
Now you seeing by the way,
literally the day after it broke

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:19.866
some other woman accused him.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.840
So is that one rape rape?

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.088
I just wanna make sure we're clear.

00:03:23.088 --> 00:03:25.970
- But what do you make of
the idea that they never

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.290
get these things turned on them?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.430
That's what was so shocking
to me, nobody does it

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.860
even though we all know it.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.930
- Correct, and it was
funny 'cause I see that.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:35.230
I mean in the last couple days
doing these book signings.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.580
Even these guys will
come to the book signing.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.170
They'll be like I love
what you did on The View.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.400
I'm like, what were you
doing watching The View?

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.646
They're like uh, uh.

00:03:41.646 --> 00:03:44.004
(laughing)

00:03:44.004 --> 00:03:45.440
It was sort of funny turning that around.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.520
But I think what it is honestly, Dave,

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.510
so many people are used
to going on those shows.

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.760
They have big viewerships,
they have big following.

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:55.030
They want to get invited back.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.517
They're there to pitch
something, as was I.

00:03:56.517 --> 00:03:59.360
I mean I didn't just go on there for fun.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.100
They're there to pitch something
so they're so desperate

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.920
about wanting to be invited
back that even though

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.910
it was their 5,000th episode,
I don't think anyone's

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:09.540
ever pushed back on them.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.500
They can sort of say
it's The View, not views.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.812
There's one view and if you don't have it

00:04:15.812 --> 00:04:17.680
they're gonna go after you.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.437
So I guess I just sort
of took their script on

00:04:19.437 --> 00:04:21.460
and people were like well how
much did you prep for this?

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.293
I didn't prep for that.

00:04:22.293 --> 00:04:24.020
I literally, like you know what?

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:25.380
Let me have something in my back pocket.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.900
If we can have a civil
discourse that's great.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.280
If we can talk about it and again,

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.384
understanding that this can be done.

00:04:29.384 --> 00:04:30.490
- So truly it was not your
intention to flip it on them?

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.540
- No, I sort of held off, but
it was like they went at me

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.877
so hard I figured hey, if
I'm on for three segments,

00:04:35.877 --> 00:04:39.290
hey we'll talk a little bit
and then they'll get rough.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:42.060
But just the opening
salvo's just aggressive.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.680
Even the conservatives
sort of come at you.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.726
So I was like okay, game on, I can play.

00:04:46.726 --> 00:04:49.500
So I didn't prep but I went on Google.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.073
I was like stupidest things
ever said on The View.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:58.210
This was not a well-researched
counterattack measure.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.170
But it was good to have
something in my back pocket

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.580
that shows a lot of that hypocrisy.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:03.880
- What does that tell you more broadly

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:04.713
about the media though,

00:05:04.713 --> 00:05:07.220
that they usually know
they can sort of say

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.053
whatever they want?

00:05:08.053 --> 00:05:09.240
And I don't mean just The View hosts.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.880
But basically sort of all the lefty media

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:12.855
can say whatever they want.

00:05:12.855 --> 00:05:15.780
You guys just sort of
take the hits usually.

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.550
And then the media then will
cover their tracks after.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:19.990
That's sort of the game that I think

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.823
a lot of this book is about.

00:05:20.823 --> 00:05:22.290
- Most people won't even go.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:24.150
Most people are afraid
of the confrontation

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:26.700
on a live screen and stuff like that.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:29.340
They're concerned.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:30.920
The different between me and so many pe--,

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.920
like I don't care what the media says.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:35.680
Some of the guys that I
spend a lot of time with

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.930
now in politics and stuff,
they've literally have

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.733
reporters call like what is it?

00:05:40.733 --> 00:05:43.590
Don, he just doesn't seem
to mind when we attack?

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.780
Like because I don't, it
means absolutely nothing.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.060
- Where do you think that
comes, do you think that's

00:05:47.060 --> 00:05:48.785
directly from your dad?

00:05:48.785 --> 00:05:51.590
- Listen, I've been used to it.

00:05:51.590 --> 00:05:53.380
I think there's a genetic component.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.440
I sort of joke in the book.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.874
I say it took us probably
41 years to realize

00:05:56.874 --> 00:05:58.530
we were much more like each other

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.850
than you would have
thought with my hobbies,

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:00.980
the outdoors, the this.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.600
My sleeping on couches in the
Midwest, that's not his thing.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:05.680
He doesn't understand that.

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:09.180
So I think if anyone would have asked us

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.030
prior to sort of the
viciousness of politics

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.740
they would have been like
Don's the one that's probably

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.573
least likely.

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:17.530
Now it was like well they
kind of fight the same way.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:18.455
You've backed us in a corner,

00:06:18.455 --> 00:06:22.870
you attack us for three
years mercilessly, we fight.

00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.140
And you know, I guess
that's the difference.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.510
It just doesn't bother me that much.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.300
So I don't really care what
other people think of me.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.275
It's never been something
that's phased me that much.

00:06:32.275 --> 00:06:36.520
So I'll get my part out and
whatever they say, they say.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:38.210
I don't freak out if I get bad press.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.252
I get bad press every day.

00:06:39.252 --> 00:06:43.362
Anything I do and say
can be used against me.

00:06:43.362 --> 00:06:45.630
This is relevant because
it's literally today,

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:46.463
Veteran's Day.

00:06:46.463 --> 00:06:49.902
In the book I wrote, there's
a chapter about sort of

00:06:49.902 --> 00:06:51.270
the victory.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.220
And I say after two years of
sort of that just fighting

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.440
during the campaign, when
we won on election night

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.080
I was not at all excited about it.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.490
It wasn't like we won a
hockey game and it's like yes,

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:03.120
two hours of--.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.655
- [Dave] Yeah, you're more like oh shit.

00:07:04.655 --> 00:07:05.488
- It was so vicious.

00:07:05.488 --> 00:07:09.388
The ups and downs, the ebbs
and flows, they're so intense

00:07:09.388 --> 00:07:11.260
it wears you down, it beats you down.

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:13.466
So when we won and they're like we got it,

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:15.550
I'm pacing around like a caged animal.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:18.640
Like no no no, they're gonna do something.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:21.330
They're gonna take what
Hillary said Trump supporters

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.820
were gonna do, they're
gonna do exactly that.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:23.950
Turned out I was right.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.620
Meaning they were gonna try to contend.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:27.617
They were gonna protest in the streets.

00:07:27.617 --> 00:07:29.852
That's what she's saying
Trump supporters are gonna do.

00:07:29.852 --> 00:07:31.570
- They're not gonna accept the results.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.792
- 100%, so I was there like no no no.

00:07:33.792 --> 00:07:34.710
I figured this game out now.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.262
They are gonna do something.

00:07:36.262 --> 00:07:41.262
So when John Podesta got
on stage and was like well,

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:44.290
I was happier about that
even though it meant

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:46.270
we were still fighting and it wasn't over,

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:51.270
than I was that we had won which
is a pretty warped reality.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:53.024
But again, two years of--

00:07:53.024 --> 00:07:54.540
- What was that night like though?

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.990
Because Hillary didn't concede that night.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.820
- Well she did, she did
later on that night.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.909
- Well she did and sort of didn't.

00:07:58.909 --> 00:08:00.360
- Yeah, it was sort of a
wishy-washy concession.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.080
Then it was like let's see
if we can pull some recounts.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.763
Turns out that we actually got
more votes in the recounts.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.780
So I wasn't at all psyched.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.050
It didn't hit me yet what
we had won and accomplished.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:14.790
So I write a chapter in the
book saying when it hit me

00:08:14.790 --> 00:08:17.130
was literally like
two-and-a-half months later.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:18.780
And it was rolling into Arlington

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.060
for the wreath-laying ceremony.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.910
And I was like I'm not an
overly-emotional kind of guy.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.690
Like I said I can kind of
compartmentalize the hate

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.830
and just move on.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.029
But dude, it hit me pretty hard.

00:08:30.029 --> 00:08:33.199
We're rolling into Arlington
and you see the gravity

00:08:33.199 --> 00:08:36.160
of the responsibility
that is what my father

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.323
has to do right now.

00:08:40.177 --> 00:08:41.341
I was so happy then.

00:08:41.341 --> 00:08:45.130
It all hit me then because
he's the guy in charge.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:46.530
I know he's gonna be such a good leader.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.950
I know he's going to get
out of these endless wars.

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.230
And you're seeing it and
some guy in the left wing

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:52.449
tries, takes some of it.

00:08:52.449 --> 00:08:54.613
He compared his sacrifices.

00:08:54.613 --> 00:08:57.480
Everything, all the B.S.
that we've been going through

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.360
100% worth it because he's the leader now

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.130
that we need.

00:09:01.130 --> 00:09:03.540
And they tried to make it
seem as though like I was

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:06.510
obviously saying that my
sacrifices as a business,

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:09.180
as a person over a campaign was the same

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.564
as the death of Americans.

00:09:10.564 --> 00:09:13.520
I was like honestly I can't even engage

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:14.670
because they'll try to build.

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.690
But no reasonable person
outside of Left Wing

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.804
and Vanity Fair and these loser
pubs that will try to take

00:09:20.804 --> 00:09:22.952
anything you say and dunk on you,

00:09:22.952 --> 00:09:25.640
no reasonable human being of the thousands

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.450
that have reached out to
me that love the book,

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:31.950
not one has even thought
that what they're saying

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:33.970
I must have meant was what I meant.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.410
I don't think any reasonable person would.

00:09:35.410 --> 00:09:37.404
But that's what they will
do and that's the sickness

00:09:37.404 --> 00:09:39.950
that is really out there in the media.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.931
- In a weird way, though, do
you guys kind of need that now?

00:09:42.931 --> 00:09:44.050
You know what I mean?

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.330
It's sort of become this
self-fulfilling prophesy.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.980
It's like the media is awful.

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.410
Everyone watching this knows that.

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:52.780
They keep doubling down on lies and racist

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:53.790
and homophobe and all that nonsense.

00:09:53.790 --> 00:09:55.900
And we'll get to all that.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.460
- I wasn't talking with
you before we ever got

00:09:57.460 --> 00:09:58.293
into politics, right?

