by not saying his name?

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.020
I mean I'm tempted to say his name.

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:34.430
- I don't know that that
matters because anyone can go on

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.210
right now and just type
it in and figure it out

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.043
for themselves.

00:20:37.043 --> 00:20:39.060
So I'd rather frankly keep the platform.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.676
But again the whole point of this--

00:20:40.676 --> 00:20:41.750
- You don't want me to
ruin my entire career

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.245
right this second just to--

00:20:43.245 --> 00:20:45.990
- Let's give them a little bit more.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:48.220
But I mean it's so much a part of the book

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.904
which is that social media censorship.

00:20:49.904 --> 00:20:53.098
They have decided, like
the mainstream media,

00:20:53.098 --> 00:20:56.480
to be the marketing arm
of the Democrat party,

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.460
all those leftist policies.

00:20:57.460 --> 00:20:59.020
- How do you think they coordinate it?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:00.280
Something like this where it's so

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.520
everything that you just said is correct.

00:21:01.520 --> 00:21:03.884
The picture is there,
obviously all the connections

00:21:03.884 --> 00:21:07.430
and no one wants anything
bad to happen to this guy.

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:08.263
- No, but they pretend.

00:21:08.263 --> 00:21:09.434
Hey I wish they would have shown,

00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:11.390
you're endangering his life.

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:13.230
I'm endangering the life of a CIA.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:16.300
I wish I would have seen one
percent, just one percent,

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.900
I don't need it all, of
the same amount of outrage

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:23.830
when my wife opened up an
exploding, white powder envelope

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:26.250
of people that was a Warren volunteer.

00:21:26.250 --> 00:21:27.610
None of that stuff comes out.

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:30.403
Like that's at my house, my kids.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.590
That doesn't deserve outrage.

00:21:33.590 --> 00:21:35.280
But this guy that's
working in the deep state,

00:21:35.280 --> 00:21:38.010
he's a CIA guy, he needs our protection.

00:21:38.010 --> 00:21:39.260
It's like give me a break.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.450
Come on, I'm not advocating
for violence of anyone.

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:45.900
But at least balance this
thing out in terms of that.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.810
So it's sort of that
outrage that just shows

00:21:48.810 --> 00:21:50.130
exactly what we're up against.

00:21:50.130 --> 00:21:52.870
- Do you think your dad
always saw that thing,

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.730
like that sort of protection racket

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:57.680
between the Democrats and the media?

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.178
It seems like he always kinda.

00:21:59.178 --> 00:22:01.635
- No one knew how to play
the media better than him

00:22:01.635 --> 00:22:04.750
when he was in his career.

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.620
I talk about in the book when we went down

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:11.620
to launch the campaign and it
was I guess June, 16, 2015.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.270
The last thing he said to
us before he walked over

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:17.676
to go to the elevator and
we went down to go watch was

00:22:17.676 --> 00:22:20.580
now we find out who our real friends are.

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:22.730
So he knows, he understand the real world.

00:22:22.730 --> 00:22:23.750
He understands how it works.

00:22:23.750 --> 00:22:25.800
He understands how full of
crap most people really are,

00:22:25.800 --> 00:22:26.760
you know what I mean?

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:28.710
Everyone's looking for
an angle and honestly

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:30.040
politics is no different.

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:33.100
If anything it's probably
worse in that effect.

00:22:33.100 --> 00:22:35.900
Meaning you're great and
you're useful until you're not.

00:22:37.950 --> 00:22:40.243
The thing that is missing
so much is loyalty.

00:22:40.243 --> 00:22:44.490
You see it and so he's always known

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:47.900
and we've always known that the
media has been left leaning.

00:22:47.900 --> 00:22:49.920
It's just now that they've
given up the pretense

00:22:49.920 --> 00:22:50.910
of even objectivity.

00:22:50.910 --> 00:22:52.410
I mean you see that.

00:22:52.410 --> 00:22:57.410
The Washington Post, the
day after the inauguration,

00:22:57.490 --> 00:22:59.570
sorry, 19 minutes after the inauguration.

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:02.000
19 minutes wrote the first article,

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.290
The Case for Impeachment.

00:23:04.290 --> 00:23:05.394
I mean 19 minutes?

00:23:05.394 --> 00:23:07.760
That's about the amount of time Obama took

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:10.845
to get nominated for the
Nobel Peace Prize, right?

00:23:10.845 --> 00:23:11.990
That was 11 days, I believe.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.300
But that's the difference, right?

00:23:15.300 --> 00:23:17.380
So when people ask what
about the impeachment

00:23:17.380 --> 00:23:18.213
that started last week?

00:23:18.213 --> 00:23:19.610
I go it didn't start last week.

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:22.937
It started on November 9,
2016, okay the day they knew

00:23:22.937 --> 00:23:24.920
he had won.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.070
This is when this thing started.

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:29.520
And you know, again if
you weren't a believer

00:23:29.520 --> 00:23:34.520
in the deep state prior
to his election, I get it.

00:23:35.667 --> 00:23:38.610
If you aren't now,
you're a freaking idiot.

00:23:38.610 --> 00:23:40.620
- Can you describe so
people say deep state

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:43.170
and then Twitter's gonna
explode in conspiracy theories.

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:46.360
You basically mean the
layer that always exists

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:48.994
because that's kind of
what kept the machine going

00:23:48.994 --> 00:23:50.400
regardless of the administration.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:54.425
- Essentially manipulating
the people's choice.

00:23:54.425 --> 00:23:57.010
Donald Trump was elected by
the people of this country.

00:23:57.010 --> 00:24:02.010
This is the unelected
self-appointed leaders

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:03.123
of this country.

00:24:03.123 --> 00:24:05.180
If they disagree with the
president who was elected

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:07.880
to do the things that he
campaigned on well we're just

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:10.360
gonna do that because we know better.

00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:13.840
And it's that class, it's
that elite, and honestly

00:24:13.840 --> 00:24:15.120
that's always existed.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:19.920
But I think now that class
is not only just existed

00:24:19.920 --> 00:24:21.580
but they've become nefarious.

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:24.047
They are doing whatever
they can to not only

00:24:24.047 --> 00:24:27.970
do their little thing, but
subvert the actual will

00:24:27.970 --> 00:24:28.803
of the people.

00:24:28.803 --> 00:24:29.810
That's where it starts getting scary.

00:24:29.810 --> 00:24:31.120
- Do you think your dad was the only guy

00:24:31.120 --> 00:24:31.953
that could break this?

00:24:31.953 --> 00:24:33.333
Because there's a lot
of metaphors for this.

00:24:33.333 --> 00:24:34.940
There's a lot of analogies.

00:24:34.940 --> 00:24:36.899
Some people say he was the
icebreaker that was gonna

00:24:36.899 --> 00:24:37.927
break it's own.

00:24:37.927 --> 00:24:39.780
Are we saying he was just the chess board?

00:24:39.780 --> 00:24:41.810
He was the guy who was just
like you're all playing

00:24:41.810 --> 00:24:42.800
this fake game.

00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:43.983
We're gonna toss it up
and see what happens.

00:24:43.983 --> 00:24:45.820
- It's probably a combination of the both.

00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:47.760
I think the reality is
if you look at sort of

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:50.007
some of the major examples
of this presidency,

00:24:50.007 --> 00:24:53.220
take Cavanaugh.

00:24:53.220 --> 00:24:57.520
How long do you think let's
say like a Jeb Bush character

00:24:57.520 --> 00:24:58.593
under fire.

00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:03.540
Unfounded, ridiculous
allegations about gang rape

00:25:03.540 --> 00:25:04.653
magically appear.

00:25:07.291 --> 00:25:09.860
How long do you think
Jeb would have lasted

00:25:09.860 --> 00:25:12.470
when the media took the
sound bites they wanted.

00:25:12.470 --> 00:25:14.230
This definitely happened 100%.

00:25:14.230 --> 00:25:15.580
We're never gonna question.

00:25:17.354 --> 00:25:18.950
A second, maybe two?

00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:21.176
That's where I'd set the
over-under before he folded.

00:25:21.176 --> 00:25:22.059
It would have ruined this guy's life.

00:25:22.059 --> 00:25:22.892
- It wouldn't have made
it those 19 minutes.

00:25:22.892 --> 00:25:24.560
- It wouldn't have made it 19 minutes.

00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:29.560
So Donald Trump just isn't
gonna buy into the nonsense.

00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:31.710
He isn't just gonna cave
to that kind of pressure.

00:25:31.710 --> 00:25:33.638
That's exactly what we need
today because we need to really

00:25:33.638 --> 00:25:36.610
reset this whole thing.

00:25:36.610 --> 00:25:39.430
So he is the perfect vessel for this.

00:25:39.430 --> 00:25:40.710
That's why when people
are like well you know,

00:25:40.710 --> 00:25:43.090
it's pretty aggressive, I'm
like we've been under attack

00:25:43.090 --> 00:25:44.400
for three years.

00:25:44.400 --> 00:25:47.680
I mean I see a lot of
moderate Democrats like

00:25:47.680 --> 00:25:49.870
honestly I'm a Democrat but
I wish they'd just let him

00:25:49.870 --> 00:25:50.703
do his job.

00:25:50.703 --> 00:25:53.966
I mean he's accomplished
things that prior pres--,

00:25:53.966 --> 00:25:57.280
Obama, had he gotten the
job numbers where they are,

00:25:57.280 --> 00:25:59.330
had he done the things for
the African American community

00:25:59.330 --> 00:26:01.510
like prison reform, opportunity zones,

00:26:01.510 --> 00:26:03.940
they would have knighted
him emperor for life.

00:26:03.940 --> 00:26:05.780
- [Dave] He's doing
this racist thing wrong.

00:26:05.780 --> 00:26:07.850
- He's like the worst racist
ever because he's failing

00:26:07.850 --> 00:26:08.683
miserably.

00:26:08.683 --> 00:26:10.480
I mean if you're gonna fail at something

00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:12.195
it's great to fail at being a racist.

00:26:12.195 --> 00:26:13.890
But it's such nonsense.

00:26:13.890 --> 00:26:15.729
I see that because I see
it from the characters.

00:26:15.729 --> 00:26:18.180
Whoopi Goldberg, we used that example.

00:26:18.180 --> 00:26:19.580
She can't say his name.

00:26:19.580 --> 00:26:21.460
Didn't stop her from showing
up at one of the finales

00:26:21.460 --> 00:26:22.780
of The Apprentice and hanging out with us

00:26:22.780 --> 00:26:26.750
at the after party five, six
years ago whenever that was.

00:26:26.750 --> 00:26:28.630
She was there, she didn't
have a problem with us then.

00:26:28.630 --> 00:26:31.260
That was another thing
I could have brought up.

00:26:31.260 --> 00:26:33.260
I mean there's just so
many examples of this.

00:26:33.260 --> 00:26:35.210
It didn't stop Al Sharpton
from saying all these

00:26:35.210 --> 00:26:36.043
complimentary things.

00:26:36.043 --> 00:26:39.030
Rev. Jesse Jackson for
saying hey, he gave us space

00:26:39.030 --> 00:26:42.443
on a Wall Street building
when we weren't anything.

00:26:42.443 --> 00:26:46.350
I have pictures with half
of the resistance at dinner.

00:26:46.350 --> 00:26:47.700
- So that's what your dad meant by the

00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:49.010
we're gonna find out who our friends are

00:26:49.010 --> 00:26:51.320
because he basically had
connections with everybody

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:52.153
in that world.

00:26:52.153 --> 00:26:55.120
- He knew he had done so
much and that's the reality.

00:26:55.120 --> 00:26:57.740
When Al Sharpton needed a
place to stay in New York,

00:26:57.740 --> 00:26:58.868
this is one of the stories in the book,

00:26:58.868 --> 00:27:02.050
he literally called me to
set him up with a broker

00:27:02.050 --> 00:27:04.360
to help get him a place.

00:27:04.360 --> 00:27:05.330
There wasn't this hatred.

00:27:05.330 --> 00:27:06.760
So they'll joke, oh we're frenemies.

00:27:06.760 --> 00:27:08.860
It's all an act.

00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:10.680
You know, they gotta play
their role, I get it.

00:27:10.680 --> 00:27:12.960
You know what I mean?

00:27:12.960 --> 00:27:14.550
It's all sort of an act.

00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:17.420
We see each other at a cigar
club I go to occasionally

00:27:17.420 --> 00:27:19.080
and we'll sit there and joke around.

00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:20.780
I know he's not on my side politically.

00:27:20.780 --> 00:27:24.990
But that we are somehow
have been oppressing them

00:27:24.990 --> 00:27:26.633
for dec--, it's nonsense.

00:27:29.804 --> 00:27:30.637
We had good relations.

00:27:30.637 --> 00:27:32.420
He'd been up in my father's
office dozens of times

00:27:32.420 --> 00:27:33.530
throughout his career.

00:27:33.530 --> 00:27:36.340
- Is part of that that if you
were to look at your resume,

00:27:36.340 --> 00:27:38.740
your lifestyle, your the
son of a billionaire,

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:40.230
you grew up in New York.

00:27:40.230 --> 00:27:43.263
You're sort of supposed to be a Democrat.

00:27:43.263 --> 00:27:47.516
- 100%, I always say that I'm
an unlikely Republican, right?

00:27:47.516 --> 00:27:50.950
I grew up in New York City,
I have a billionaire father.

00:27:50.950 --> 00:27:52.740
I went to an Ivy League
school, all these things.

00:27:52.740 --> 00:27:55.985
And the big part I talk about
that is sort of the lessons

00:27:55.985 --> 00:27:57.890
I've seen throughout life.

00:27:57.890 --> 00:27:59.930
I learned about sort of
that socialist movement

00:27:59.930 --> 00:28:02.040
especially as I see the
Democrat party going really

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:05.990
towards welcoming sort of
socialism, communist ideals.

00:28:05.990 --> 00:28:07.910
It's no longer a fringe
element of the party,

00:28:07.910 --> 00:28:10.400
it's literally the leading
people are like hey,

00:28:10.400 --> 00:28:13.120
we're vacationing in the Soviet
Union, this is wonderful.

00:28:13.120 --> 00:28:14.887
- If only someone had
been talking about this

00:28:14.887 --> 00:28:16.170
for the last three years.

00:28:16.170 --> 00:28:18.780
- Exactly well that was
one of the big reasons

00:28:18.780 --> 00:28:20.750
to write the book which
is like I hate watching

00:28:20.750 --> 00:28:23.780
these people that talk
about the great ideals

00:28:23.780 --> 00:28:27.830
of socialism who have never
actually lived under it.

00:28:27.830 --> 00:28:29.600
Again I've got to caveat everything.

00:28:29.600 --> 00:28:30.890
I'm the son of a rich
guy (mumbles), I get it.

00:28:30.890 --> 00:28:33.493
But my mother escaped
Communist Czechoslovakia.

00:28:34.380 --> 00:28:37.080
You know, I had a
grandfather, a grandmother

00:28:37.080 --> 00:28:38.980
that lived under all of that nonsense.

00:28:40.240 --> 00:28:42.340
And I had the good fortune
of them recognizing

00:28:42.340 --> 00:28:44.900
the blessings that we
have here in this country.

00:28:44.900 --> 00:28:48.060
So they, from a young age
I spoke Czech fluently.

00:28:48.060 --> 00:28:49.497
My grandfather would be
like hey, he's got to see

00:28:49.497 --> 00:28:50.330
the other side.

00:28:50.330 --> 00:28:51.730
You have it really good here.

00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:53.260
Just to never take anything for granted.

00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:54.700
Just to never have that.

00:28:54.700 --> 00:28:56.680
So he would take me over
there starting at like

00:28:56.680 --> 00:29:01.110
the age of five for four
to six weeks every summer.

00:29:01.110 --> 00:29:02.070
I had friends over there.

00:29:02.070 --> 00:29:03.550
I've waiting in those bread lines, Dave.

00:29:03.550 --> 00:29:05.131
I can assure you there's
nothing less glamorous

00:29:05.131 --> 00:29:07.670
than an empty supermarket.

00:29:07.670 --> 00:29:08.990
This wasn't like a helicopter generation.

00:29:08.990 --> 00:29:09.823
I may have been five or six.

00:29:09.823 --> 00:29:13.253
You're going to the corner
store and waiting for bread.

00:29:14.090 --> 00:29:15.603
I've done that.

00:29:15.603 --> 00:29:17.670
I saw as a kid, I'd be
like why is my grandmother

00:29:17.670 --> 00:29:19.190
not in my parents wedding picture?

00:29:19.190 --> 00:29:20.580
It was like my grandfather.

00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:23.320
Well they let him out of the
country to walk his daughter

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:25.070
down the aisle, but they
wouldn't let the wife

00:29:25.070 --> 00:29:27.300
for fear that they would defect.

00:29:27.300 --> 00:29:29.050
What kind of system
doesn't let people leave

00:29:29.050 --> 00:29:31.063
because they know they ain't coming back?

00:29:32.070 --> 00:29:33.720
So I've experienced these things.

00:29:35.580 --> 00:29:38.030
To see them pushed as
mainstream thought now

00:29:38.030 --> 00:29:38.970
it's really scary.

00:29:38.970 --> 00:29:41.230
I remember that my first memory of fear

00:29:41.230 --> 00:29:43.300
that I talk about in the
book was going over there

00:29:43.300 --> 00:29:44.133
the first time.

00:29:44.133 --> 00:29:44.966
I was wearing like, it was pretty cool

00:29:44.966 --> 00:29:46.460
because it was the 80s.

00:29:46.460 --> 00:29:49.010
I was wearing a blue jean
jacket with the stars

00:29:49.010 --> 00:29:50.160
and stripes on it.

00:29:50.160 --> 00:29:51.260
It was kind of 80s.

00:29:51.260 --> 00:29:52.600
- [Dave] Yeah, Rocky.

00:29:52.600 --> 00:29:55.660
- I got pulled out of
the line by a customs guy

00:29:55.660 --> 00:29:58.090
in a military thing with
an AK over his shoulder.

00:29:58.090 --> 00:29:59.130
He started questioning me.

00:29:59.130 --> 00:30:04.030
Like was I there to
preach the great aspects

00:30:04.030 --> 00:30:04.863
of capitalism?

00:30:04.863 --> 00:30:06.160
I'm like dude, I'm five years old.

00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:08.010
And not like one of today's five year olds

00:30:08.010 --> 00:30:09.090
who are much more woke.

00:30:09.090 --> 00:30:10.342
They're asking about
nuclear proliferation.

00:30:10.342 --> 00:30:11.695
You see this on Twitter all the time.

00:30:11.695 --> 00:30:16.520
My two-and-a-half year old
asking me about the dangers

00:30:16.520 --> 00:30:18.870
of nuclear proliferation
in the Korean peninsula

00:30:18.870 --> 00:30:21.240
and its effect on macroeconomics.

00:30:21.240 --> 00:30:22.073
No, I was five.

00:30:22.073 --> 00:30:23.960
- It's incredible it always
happens to those blue check--.

00:30:23.960 --> 00:30:26.040
- It's always the blue check mark kids.

00:30:26.040 --> 00:30:27.900
They're really woke, and
I'm like it's amazing

00:30:27.900 --> 00:30:31.080
how it just fits into the byline of today.

00:30:31.080 --> 00:30:33.130
- None of your kids have
asked you about string theory?

00:30:33.130 --> 00:30:35.820
- No they haven't, they haven't.

00:30:35.820 --> 00:30:38.900
Hard to believe, I guess
they're just not that smart.

00:30:38.900 --> 00:30:39.733
It's a shame.

00:30:39.733 --> 00:30:42.934
I was really hoping they
would be Ph.D's at four.

00:30:42.934 --> 00:30:44.350
- You've got to get them
to a more elite school.

00:30:44.350 --> 00:30:45.183
That's the problem.

00:30:45.183 --> 00:30:46.016
- I know, it's a shame.

00:30:46.016 --> 00:30:48.070
So I've seen that stuff, I've lived it.

00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:49.900
My 93-year old grandmother is still alive.

