00:43:30.168 --> 00:43:33.220
He's a brilliant guy, he's a
brilliant guy so he manages

00:43:33.220 --> 00:43:35.380
to rise through the ranks
there faster than anyone.

00:43:35.380 --> 00:43:37.040
Obviously totally a coincidence.

00:43:37.040 --> 00:43:40.280
He then gets a board seat on Amtrak at 27.

00:43:40.280 --> 00:43:42.430
Huge, he's a lover of trains.

00:43:42.430 --> 00:43:44.680
He's a lover of trains obviously, Dave.

00:43:44.680 --> 00:43:46.300
I mean that's why he got it.

00:43:46.300 --> 00:43:49.010
Nothing to do with daddy
controlling the purse strings.

00:43:49.010 --> 00:43:50.600
No no no, that's off limits.

00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.420
I haven't talked much
about it because honestly

00:43:52.420 --> 00:43:53.440
it's not even worth it.

00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:55.760
But you get frustrated enough
'cause they have to attack

00:43:55.760 --> 00:43:57.187
